@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Private workspace restore: guarded replacement and failure paths
start
:Signed-in owner selects backup ZIP;
:Validate byte limits, paths, manifest,\nrecord schema and referenced audio;
if (Archive valid?) then (yes)
  :Show counts and replacement warning;\nstore one-hour owner-scoped preview;
else (no)
  :Report validation error;\nleave live data unchanged;
  stop
endif
if (Owner types REPLACE and confirms?) then (yes)
  :Acquire account workspace lock;
else (no)
  :Keep current workspace;\npreview expires without applying it;
  stop
endif
if (Preview valid and version unchanged?) then (yes)
  :Revalidate archive and create\nverified pre-restore safety backup;
else (no)
  :Release lock; report expiry/conflict;
  stop
endif
if (Safety backup succeeded?) then (yes)
  :Stage missing audio immutably;\nremap conflicting filenames;
else (no)
  :Release lock; report failure;\nleave logical data unchanged;
  stop
endif
if (Audio staging succeeded?) then (yes)
  :Replace logical rows in one\nversion-checked SQLite transaction;
else (no)
  :Remove only newly staged files;\nrelease lock and report failure;
  stop
endif
if (Transaction committed?) then (yes)
  :Invalidate preview; retain safety backup\nand previous committed media;
  if (Post-commit cleanup succeeded?) then (yes)
    :Release lock; reopen General;\nreview restored information;
  else (no)
    :Release lock; report uncertain completion;\nrefresh saved state, do not restore blindly;
  endif
else (no)
  :Rollback rows; remove newly staged files;\nrelease lock and report failure;
endif
stop
legend bottom
  Branch guards are exclusive; each final node ends this attempt.
  A cleanup error is explicit and does not imply a committed transaction rolled back.
  This activity does not delete account credentials or other users' workspaces.
endlegend
@enduml
